WHY THIS RATHER THAN MIT OR APACHE-2.0
--------------------------------------

Those licences are irrevocable for the version they were applied to: publishing
one release under MIT permits commercial use of that release permanently, and
re-licensing later cannot withdraw it. This project may be commercialised, so
that door is deliberately left shut. A file saying nothing would have the same
legal effect by default — every right reserved — but it leaves readers guessing
whether that was intended, so this states it.

If you want to use any of this, ask. Permission is likely and free for
non-commercial use; it just has to be granted rather than assumed.

